      "message": "nit: s/sensitve/sensitive/\n\n...But actually, this comment is IMO a bit too specific. pKVM must protect any pVM pages even if they don\u0027t happen to contain sensitive data, that is pKVM\u0027s job.\n\nAlso, if a device can write to those pages, it is just as bad as if it can read them.\n\nAlso, exactly the same applies to donating pages to the hypervisor, not just to a pVM.\n\nSo maybe just something like: \"Regardless of the DMA mode used by host (i.e. strict or lazy), always perform iotlb flush on unmap. Unmapped pages may be donated to a pVM or to the hypervisor. Until a flush happens, stale entries in the IOTLB could enable a device to access those pages, violating isolation guarantees.\" ?",
